# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile bosonic circuits {#transpile-bosonic-circuits}"
msgstr "Transpilar circuitos bosónicos {#transpile-bosonic-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This guide explains how to transpile a [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") to a standard [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). A bosonic circuit carries no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit count (see [Work with bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), so the transpiler is where those choices are made. The truncation and the encoding are described by a [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") (see [Describe the truncation with a LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)), and the mapper that turns operators into qubit operators is described in [Map operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation). The result is an ordinary [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit), so any Qiskit-compatible simulator can run it.\n"
msgstr "Esta guía explica cómo transpilar un [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") a un [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) estándar. Un circuito bosónico no lleva truncamiento, ni codificación, ni número de qubits (consulta [Trabajar con circuitos bosónicos](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation)), así que el transpilador es donde se toman esas decisiones. El truncamiento y la codificación los describe un [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") (consulta [Describir el truncamiento con un LevelSpec](mappers#level-spec-explanation)), y el mapper que convierte operadores en operadores de qubits se describe en [Asignar representaciones de operadores](mappers#mappers-explanation). El resultado es un [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit) corriente, por lo que cualquier simulador compatible con Qiskit puede ejecutarlo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The guide uses one small example throughout: two bosonic modes, a state with one boson in each, and a single time evolution under a Bose-Hubbard Hamiltonian whose bond and on-site terms are in separate groups (see [Group operator terms: use the operator structure](grouping#grouping-explanation)):\n"
msgstr "La guía usa un pequeño ejemplo de principio a fin: dos modos bosónicos, un estado con un bosón en cada uno y una única evolución temporal bajo un hamiltoniano de Bose-Hubbard cuyos términos de enlace y de sitio están en grupos separados (consulta [Agrupar términos de operadores: usar la estructura del operador](grouping#grouping-explanation)):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpilation stages {#transpilation-stages}"
msgstr "Etapas de la transpilación {#transpilation-stages}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As explained in [`qiskit_bosons.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler#module-qiskit_bosons.transpiler \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler\"), the preset pass managers in this package split the transpilation into the following stages:\n"
msgstr "Como se explica en [`qiskit_bosons.transpiler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler#module-qiskit_bosons.transpiler \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler\"), los pass managers predefinidos de este paquete dividen la transpilación en las siguientes etapas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Input** {#input}"
msgstr "**Entrada** {#input}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts the circuit to a directed acyclic graph (DAG) data structure, the representation that every later pass works on.\n"
msgstr "Convierte el circuito en una estructura de datos de grafo acíclico dirigido (DAG), la representación sobre la que trabaja cada pasada posterior.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Optimization** {#optimization}"
msgstr "**Optimización** {#optimization}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keeps the circuit in bosonic space. These passes use the structure of the bosonic operators, in particular their groups, while no qubit information exists yet. [`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") is the pass that breaks gates down here, with a plugin for each type of gate: a product formula or qDRIFT for an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\"), and the Clements mesh for a [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") (see [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) for how a method is chosen). [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") reorders the modes. The preset decomposes mode rotations in this stage and leaves everything else as it is.\n"
msgstr "Mantiene el circuito en el espacio bosónico. Estas pasadas usan la estructura de los operadores bosónicos, en particular sus grupos, mientras aún no existe información de qubits. [`B2BSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-b-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2BSynthesis\") es la pasada que descompone aquí las puertas, con un plugin para cada tipo de puerta: una fórmula de producto o qDRIFT para un [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\"), y la malla de Clements para un [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") (consulta [Sintetizar una puerta Evolution en el espacio bosónico](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) para ver cómo se elige un método). [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") reordena los modos. El preajuste descompone las rotaciones de modos en esta etapa y deja todo lo demás como está.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Layout** {#layout}"
msgstr "**Disposición** {#layout}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Maps each bosonic mode register to a quantum register. A bosonic mode generally occupies several qubits ($d$ of them under the unary encodings, $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ under the compact ones), so the quantum register is wider than the mode register. [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") derives the register width from a [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\").\n"
msgstr "Asigna cada registro de modos bosónicos a un registro cuántico. Un modo bosónico generalmente ocupa varios qubits ($d$ de ellos con las codificaciones unarias, $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ con las compactas), por lo que el registro cuántico es más ancho que el registro de modos. [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") deriva el ancho del registro a partir de un [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\").\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Synthesis** {#synthesis}"
msgstr "**Síntesis** {#synthesis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts bosonic gates to qubit operations, one plugin per gate type. Encoding happens in this step: the plugin for an [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate maps its operator to a qubit operator, and the plugin for an [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") gate sets the qubits that encode each occupation. A barrier is carried onto every qubit of each register it touched.\n"
msgstr "Convierte las puertas bosónicas en operaciones de qubits, un plugin por tipo de puerta. La codificación ocurre en este paso: el plugin para una puerta [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") asigna su operador a un operador de qubits, y el plugin para una puerta [`InitializeModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-initialize-modes#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.InitializeModes\") establece los qubits que codifican cada ocupación. Una barrera se extiende a todos los qubits de cada registro que tocaba.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Qubit** {#qubit}"
msgstr "**Qubit** {#qubit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpiles the resulting qubit circuit with Qiskit’s own methods, for example to a basis gate set or a device. The preset always includes it; by default it is Qiskit’s preset pass manager, which synthesizes every evolution into gates (see [Continue on the qubit level](#transpilation-qubit-stage)).\n"
msgstr "Transpila el circuito de qubits resultante con los propios métodos de Qiskit, por ejemplo a un conjunto de puertas base o a un dispositivo. El preajuste siempre la incluye; de forma predeterminada es el pass manager predefinido de Qiskit, que sintetiza cada evolución en puertas (consulta [Continuar en el nivel de qubits](#transpilation-qubit-stage)).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Output** {#output}"
msgstr "**Salida** {#output}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Converts the internal DAG data structure back to a [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit).\n"
msgstr "Convierte la estructura de datos DAG interna de vuelta en un [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The truncation and the encoding are not stored in the circuit. They are given to the transpiler, and the layout, the state preparation, and the mapper must all agree on them. The preset ensures that by handing the same [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") to all three.\n"
msgstr "El truncamiento y la codificación no se almacenan en el circuito. Se entregan al transpilador, y la disposición, la preparación del estado y el mapper deben coincidir en ellos. El preajuste lo garantiza entregando el mismo [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") a los tres.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "A practical example {#a-practical-example}"
msgstr "Un ejemplo práctico {#a-practical-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-occupation-pass-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager\") builds the pipeline from a spec. Lowering the example under two encodings only changes the spec. The preset ends in Qiskit’s own qubit-level transpilation, which would synthesize the evolution into gates. To see the circuit exactly as the bosonic stages emit it, empty that stage first:\n"
msgstr "[`generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-occupation-pass-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager\") construye el pipeline a partir de una especificación. Reducir el ejemplo bajo dos codificaciones solo cambia la especificación. El preajuste termina en la propia transpilación a nivel de qubits de Qiskit, que sintetizaría la evolución en puertas. Para ver el circuito exactamente como lo emiten las etapas bosónicas, vacía primero esa etapa:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two encodings use six and four qubits respectively (three levels per mode under the unary encoding, two qubits per mode under the Gray code), but the structure of the circuit is the same: two [`XGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XGate) operations prepare the occupations, and one [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) carries the evolution.\n"
msgstr "Las dos codificaciones usan seis y cuatro qubits respectivamente (tres niveles por modo con la codificación unaria, dos qubits por modo con el código de Gray), pero la estructura del circuito es la misma: dos operaciones [`XGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.XGate) preparan las ocupaciones, y un [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) lleva la evolución.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare with the traditional workflow {#compare-with-the-traditional-workflow}"
msgstr "Comparación con el flujo de trabajo tradicional {#compare-with-the-traditional-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [bosonic circuits](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation) guide describes the traditional workflow, which maps the Hamiltonian to a qubit operator *before* it builds the [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). The two routes produce equivalent circuits. They differ in what has to be redone when the truncation changes. The bosonic circuit is built once and lowered at every cutoff, whereas the map-first route needs the operator mapped again and the circuit rebuilt:\n"
msgstr "La guía de [circuitos bosónicos](circuit#bosonic-circuit-explanation) describe el flujo de trabajo tradicional, que asigna el hamiltoniano a un operador de qubits *antes* de construir el [`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit). Las dos rutas producen circuitos equivalentes. Se diferencian en lo que hay que rehacer cuando cambia el truncamiento. El circuito bosónico se construye una vez y se reduce con cada corte, mientras que la ruta que asigna primero necesita volver a asignar el operador y reconstruir el circuito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entangling-gate count depends on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution gate, which changes between releases, so plot it:\n"
msgstr "El número de puertas entrelazantes depende de cómo sintetiza Qiskit la puerta de evolución, lo cual cambia entre versiones, así que represéntalo en una gráfica:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![CX count of the lowered circuit against the number of levels d, growing quickly with d.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/transpilation-4.avif)\n"
msgstr "![CX count of the lowered circuit against the number of levels d, growing quickly with d.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/transpilation-4.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The count grows quickly with the cutoff, which is the reason to keep the cutoff a parameter of the transpilation and not of the circuit. The two routes are equivalent here, but only the bosonic one can also interleave the grouping of the operator with the product formula (see [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation)) or hand the encoding to a different spec without changing a line of the circuit.\n"
msgstr "El número crece rápidamente con el corte, que es la razón para mantener el corte como parámetro de la transpilación y no del circuito. Las dos rutas son equivalentes aquí, pero solo la bosónica puede también intercalar la agrupación del operador con la fórmula de producto (consulta [Sintetizar una puerta Evolution en el espacio bosónico](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation)) o entregar la codificación a una especificación distinta sin cambiar una línea del circuito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A spec with a single cutoff leaves the number of modes open, so one pass manager serves circuits of any width. A spec with one cutoff per mode fixes the width:\n"
msgstr "Una especificación con un único corte deja abierto el número de modos, de modo que un solo pass manager sirve para circuitos de cualquier anchura. Una especificación con un corte por modo fija la anchura:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the pipeline by hand {#build-the-pipeline-by-hand}"
msgstr "Construir el pipeline a mano {#build-the-pipeline-by-hand}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The preset is a [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager) with one entry per stage. You can assemble the same pipeline from its parts, which is the starting point for every customization below:\n"
msgstr "El preset es un [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager) con una entrada por etapa. Puedes ensamblar el mismo pipeline a partir de sus partes, que es el punto de partida de todas las personalizaciones que siguen:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The mapper function receives an operator and the width of the register that the layout derived, and returns a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable). Because it is given the width, passing `num_qubits` on to [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") makes the mapper check that the spec fits the register, so a mismatch between the layout and the encoding fails with a clear message.\n"
msgstr "La función mapeadora recibe un operador y el ancho del registro que derivó el layout, y devuelve un [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable). Como recibe el ancho, pasar `num_qubits` a [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") hace que el mapeador compruebe que la especificación cabe en el registro, de modo que una discrepancia entre el layout y la codificación falla con un mensaje claro.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Advanced workflows {#advanced-workflows}"
msgstr "Flujos de trabajo avanzados {#advanced-workflows}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Provide an explicit layout {#provide-an-explicit-layout}"
msgstr "Proporciona un layout explícito {#provide-an-explicit-layout}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`CustomB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-custom-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.CustomB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.CustomB2QLayout\") replaces the layout stage with a mapping that you provide, from each bosonic register of the circuit to a quantum register. It is useful when the register must be wider than the spec needs, for example to leave idle qubits for other purposes:\n"
msgstr "[`CustomB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-custom-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.CustomB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.CustomB2QLayout\") sustituye la etapa de layout por un mapeo que tú proporcionas, desde cada registro bosónico del circuito hasta un registro cuántico. Es útil cuando el registro debe ser más ancho de lo que necesita la especificación, por ejemplo para dejar qubits inactivos para otros fines:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  A custom layout is your responsibility. The synthesis plugins still address qubits through the spec, so a register that does not match the spec’s widths gives a wrong circuit or an error deep inside a plugin. A custom layout also skips the check that [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") performs after [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") (see the next section).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Advertencia\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Un layout personalizado es responsabilidad tuya. Los plugins de síntesis siguen direccionando los qubits a través de la especificación, así que un registro que no coincide con los anchos de la especificación produce un circuito incorrecto o un error en lo profundo de un plugin. Un layout personalizado también omite la comprobación que [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") realiza después de [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") (consulta la siguiente sección).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reorder the modes {#reorder-the-modes}"
msgstr "Reordena los modos {#reorder-the-modes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") is an optimization-stage pass that reorders the modes. The permutation is read as a mapping from original to new mode index, and it is recorded in the circuit metadata. The reordering changes which qubits each mode occupies, and so it can reduce the depth of the lowered circuit.\n"
msgstr "[`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\") es un pase de la etapa de optimización que reordena los modos. La permutación se interpreta como un mapeo del índice de modo original al nuevo, y se registra en los metadatos del circuito. El reordenamiento cambia qué qubits ocupa cada modo y, por tanto, puede reducir la profundidad del circuito reducido.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the result is expressed in the new mode order, measured bitstrings must be mapped back before they are interpreted. With several qubits per mode, the mapping acts on blocks of qubits and not on single bits. The following example relabels three modes, each occupying two qubits under the Gray code, and recovers the original occupation from the measured counts:\n"
msgstr "Como el resultado se expresa en el nuevo orden de modos, las cadenas de bits medidas deben mapearse de vuelta antes de interpretarse. Con varios qubits por modo, el mapeo actúa sobre bloques de qubits y no sobre bits individuales. El siguiente ejemplo reetiqueta tres modos, cada uno ocupando dos qubits con el código Gray, y recupera la ocupación original a partir de los conteos medidos:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The restored bitstring is what the circuit produces without the relabeling, read in Qiskit’s little-endian order: mode 0 holds the Gray code of level two (`11`), mode 1 holds level zero (`00`), and mode 2 holds level one (`01`).\n"
msgstr "La cadena de bits restaurada es lo que produce el circuito sin el reetiquetado, leída en el orden little-endian de Qiskit: el modo 0 contiene el código Gray del nivel dos (`11`), el modo 1 contiene el nivel cero (`00`) y el modo 2 contiene el nivel uno (`01`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Warning\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Advertencia\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  A spec that gives the modes **different** cutoffs cannot be combined with [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\"). The cutoffs are attached to the modes by their position, so reordering the modes would put a cutoff on the wrong mode. [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") refuses a relabeled circuit in that case:\n"
msgstr "  Una especificación que asigna **distintos** cutoffs a los modos no se puede combinar con [`RelabelModes`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-relabel-modes#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.RelabelModes\"). Los cutoffs se asocian a los modos por su posición, así que reordenar los modos pondría un cutoff en el modo equivocado. [`OccupationB2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-occupation-b-2-q-layout#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.OccupationB2QLayout\") rechaza un circuito reetiquetado en ese caso:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the synthesis plugins {#choose-the-synthesis-plugins}"
msgstr "Elige los plugins de síntesis {#choose-the-synthesis-plugins}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\") has no default plugins; the preset registers one per gate type. The available plugins are managed by [`B2QSynthesisPluginManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-b-2-q-synthesis-plugin-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.B2QSynthesisPluginManager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.B2QSynthesisPluginManager\"), which lists them by the name of the gate they act on:\n"
msgstr "[`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\") no tiene plugins por defecto; el preset registra uno por tipo de compuerta. Los plugins disponibles los gestiona [`B2QSynthesisPluginManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-b-2-q-synthesis-plugin-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.B2QSynthesisPluginManager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.B2QSynthesisPluginManager\"), que los enumera por el nombre de la compuerta sobre la que actúan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two builtin methods are `Evolution.MapperFn` and `InitializeModes.Occupation`. The first synthesizes an evolution from any mapper function, which is how a custom encoding is plugged in (see [Map operator representations](mappers#mappers-explanation)). The library ships no plugin for a [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\") gate. The preset breaks it down in bosonic space into [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gates first, which the first method then handles, but a plugin registered for `ModeRotation` can lower the gate directly instead; see [Rotate bosonic modes](mode-rotation#mode-rotation-explanation) and [Lower a rotation without decomposing it](mode-rotation#mode-rotation-direct-explanation). You can register a method by name through the `config` argument of [`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\"), or write a plugin object into [`B2QSynthesis.methods`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis.methods \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis.methods\") directly, as the preceding examples do.\n"
msgstr "Los dos métodos integrados son `Evolution.MapperFn` e `InitializeModes.Occupation`. El primero sintetiza una evolución a partir de cualquier función mapeadora, que es la forma de conectar una codificación personalizada (consulta [Mapear representaciones de operadores](mappers#mappers-explanation)). La biblioteca no incluye ningún plugin para una compuerta [`ModeRotation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-mode-rotation#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.ModeRotation\"). El preset primero la descompone en el espacio bosónico en compuertas [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\"), que el primer método ya sabe tratar, pero un plugin registrado para `ModeRotation` puede reducir la compuerta directamente; consulta [Rotar modos bosónicos](mode-rotation#mode-rotation-explanation) y [Reducir una rotación sin descomponerla](mode-rotation#mode-rotation-direct-explanation). Puedes registrar un método por nombre mediante el argumento `config` de [`B2QSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis\"), o escribir un objeto plugin directamente en [`B2QSynthesis.methods`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-b-2-q-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis.methods \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.B2QSynthesis.methods\"), como hacen los ejemplos anteriores.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpilation-qubit-stage\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Continue on the qubit level {#continue-on-the-qubit-level}"
msgstr "Continúa a nivel de qubits {#continue-on-the-qubit-level}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The preset always ends in a `qubit` stage, which is Qiskit’s own preset pass manager. Keyword arguments of [`generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-occupation-pass-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager\") are handed to [`qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager), so you can translate to a basis gate set or target a device directly. Prefer `optimization_level=0` to keep the circuit close to what the bosonic stages produced:\n"
msgstr "El preset siempre termina en una etapa `qubit`, que es el pass manager preestablecido propio de Qiskit. Los argumentos de palabra clave de [`generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-presets-generate-preset-occupation-pass-manager#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.presets.generate_preset_occupation_pass_manager\") se pasan a [`qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.generate_preset_pass_manager), de modo que puedes traducir a un conjunto de compuertas base o apuntar directamente a un dispositivo. Es preferible usar `optimization_level=0` para mantener el circuito cerca de lo que produjeron las etapas bosónicas:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two other choices are common. Assign an empty [`PassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.PassManager) to the `qubit` stage when you want to show the circuit exactly as the pipeline synthesized it, as the examples above do. Or assemble the pipeline yourself and add any Qiskit pass manager as the `qubit` stage of the [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager). Stages run in the order they are given, so the `qubit` stage must come before `output`, because Qiskit’s passes expect a DAG and not a finished circuit:\n"
msgstr "Hay otras dos opciones habituales. Asigna un [`PassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.PassManager) vacío a la etapa `qubit` cuando quieras mostrar el circuito exactamente como lo sintetizó el pipeline, como hacen los ejemplos anteriores. O ensambla tú mismo el pipeline y añade cualquier pass manager de Qiskit como etapa `qubit` del [`MultiStagePassManager`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.passmanager.MultiStagePassManager). Las etapas se ejecutan en el orden en que se indican, así que la etapa `qubit` debe ir antes de `output`, porque los pases de Qiskit esperan un DAG y no un circuito terminado:\n"

